      "**Anti-Monopoly Legislation:** Laws preventing concentration of economic power (Competition Act, 2002) reflect Article 39(c) objectives.",
      "**Wealth Tax (Historical):** The now-repealed Wealth Tax Act aimed to prevent concentration of wealth — an Article 39(c) objective.",
      "**Ceiling on Property:** Urban and agricultural land ceiling laws preventing concentration of landed wealth are protected.",
      "**Public Distribution System:** The PDS, distributing essential commodities at subsidized rates, implements Article 39(b).",
      "**Nationalization of Insurance:** LIC's creation through nationalization served Article 39(b) objectives.",
      "**Bank Nationalization:** Nationalization of banks aimed at distributing credit as a material resource for the common good.",
      "**Forest and Mineral Resources:** Government control over forest and mineral resources implements Article 39(b).",
      "**Essential Commodities Price Control:** Price controls on essential goods prevent concentration and ensure distribution — Article 39(b) and (c).",
      "**Right to Food Legislation:** The National Food Security Act, 2013, distributes food as a material resource — protected by Article 31C.",
      "**Limitation by Minerva Mills:** Any law claiming Article 31C protection must genuinely implement Article 39(b) or (c) — judicial review of this nexus remains available."
